      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change is needed to allow EGits history view to load commits incrementally (Using the algorithm in Change I0a2115bfef7e73a299780a2c28ef5a01aa1d00e0).\n\nTo test incremental loading in EGit history view:\n - Recommended: Cherry pick Change I188a8f35553e00ce5b3866e254d114884dc30a68\n - Set the following git config options\n     git config core.commitgraph true\n     git config gc.writecommitgraph true\n     git config gc.writechangedpaths true\n     git config commitgraph.changedpaths true\n     git config -f ~/.config/jgit/config commitgraph.readchangedpaths true\n  - Generate a commit graph for a large repository (e.g. Linux Kernel)\n     git commit-graph write --changed-paths\n  - Set the RefFilter to \"Current Branch (Local and Remote)\"\n     - Including all tags and branches for large monorepos (like the Linux Kernel) still takes a long time to load the first batch of commits\n  - EGit History view should now immediately start listing commits\n     - Performance without a commit-graph on my machine was approximately 10 seconds loading time for the history view (using Linux Kernel Repository)",
